 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 532550,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "You want to carpet your bedroom, which measures 15 ft wide by 18 ft long. Carpeting is sold by the square yard, so you must convert your measurements to yards. How much carpeting do you buy?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>First, convert the dimensions to yards. There are 3 feet in one yard.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"15{\\text{ }}\\cancel{{{\\text{feet}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{{\\text{1 yard}}}}{{{\\text{3 }}\\cancel{{{\\text{feet}}}}}}} \\right) = 5{\\text{ yards}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"18{\\text{ }}\\cancel{{{\\text{feet}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{{\\text{1 yard}}}}{{{\\text{3 }}\\cancel{{{\\text{feet}}}}}}} \\right) = 6{\\text{ yards}}\"></span></p>\n<p>The area of a rectangle is <span data-math=\"A = LW\"></span>where <i>L</i> represents the length and <i>W</i> represents the width.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = LW = \\left( {5{\\text{ yd}}} \\right)\\left( {{\\text{6 yd}}} \\right) = 30{\\text{ y}}{{\\text{d}}^2}\"></span></p>\n<p>You need 30 square yards of carpet.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"30\\,{\\text{y}}{{\\text{d}}^2}\">30\\,{\\text{y}}{{\\text{d}}^2}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
